1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1909 - Birth and Baptism:  
2 CONT
2 CONT Source information: Østfold county, Tune, Parish register (official) nr. 20 (1904-1909), Birth and baptism records 1909, page 152, no. 59. Martha was born June 16, 1909 on Lande inTune                                              
2 CONC                      Martha was baptized July 11, 1909 in Tune kirke  Her parents lived in Lande, Tune, her father was sawmill worker Kristian Johansen Pinaas, born in 1886 and mother was Anna Sofie Johannessen, born1887.         
2 CONC                Godparents were: The child’s parents, farmer Peter Jensen Pinaas, Miss Helga Johansen Pinaas, and factory worker Hermann Martinsen Lande.   http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20060604040162.jpg
2 CONT
2 CONT 1930 - Marriage:  
2 CONT
2 CONT Source information: Østfold county, Hafslund in Skjeberg, Banns register nr. Hc 0001 (1919-1949), Banns records 1930, page 34. No 2. Martha got married January 13, 1930 in Hafslund kapell. The bridesgroom was carbide factory worke
2 CONC r Otter Øivind Grønn, born January 22, 1907 in Halden and living in Bede and the bride was seamstress Martha Kristine Pinaas living with her parents on Borgenhaugen. The bride and groom’s fathers both signed their permission of th
2 CONC e marriage on January 6, 1930.                                          Witnesses were: Mrs. Ragnhild Solveig Olsen, Bede and Locomotive operator Kristian Pinaas, Borgenhaugen.                                                      
2 CONC        http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20060327010704.jpg
2 CONT
2 CONT 1940 - Death:   Martha died in 1940 from tuberculosis, as so many other young people did at that time.  Her son Kjell also had tuberculosis in his teens, but he overcame the illness and is still alive today (2015) at the age of 82
2 CONC .  Martha’s death and burial record is not available on-line.
