1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Notes by Egil Berger (2013)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Leiv is my uncle, brother of my mother Solveig Pinaas, At the time of his birth, Leiv’s parents lived on Kjendshaug, Lande, in Tune, and his father was a cellulose worker at Borregaard. He enjoyed music and he played piano, organ 
2 CONC and bass. He also liked cars, and I remember he gave me a book describing many of the new cars.  This must have been around 1950 and I still remember how exciting it was to look at the pictures of all these beautiful and powerful 
2 CONC cars.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the oldest living son of Kristian and Anna after his brother Alf died in 1944.  It was sometime before 1950 that Leiv and Synøve took over his parents’ house at Borgenveien 3.
2 CONT
2 CONT He worked as a chauffeur most of his life.  He drove a taxi cab during the war when there was no gasoline available in Norway, and the cars were converted to run on gas provided by wood-burning generator mounted on the cars and tr
2 CONC ucks.  It worked, but the cars lost a good part of power and I remember Leiv telling me that when he drove the taxi up a steep hill the passenger(s) often had to step out and help push the taxi over the hill. He also drove for the
2 CONC  local bus company in Sarpsborg and drove the Sarpsborg-Høysand-Sarpsborg route for many years.
