1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Notes by Egil Berger 2013'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Roald Pinaas is my uncle, brother of my mother. I remember Roald always liked cars.  He bought his first car, a 1924 Ford T from a farmer at Lunde, Degernes.  He later sold this car to his brother John who needed a “pick-up” truck
2 CONC  while building his house at Skolegata on Borgenhaugen.
2 CONT
2 CONT I remember some of Roald’s cars, a Ford A, a Ford V8, a Ford Consul.  Roald worked for a while for Johs. Stamsås, his uncle (I believe and the Ford dealer) in Sarpsborg, so every car was a Ford in those days.  Is wasn’t until he b
2 CONC ought the used Mercedes from the director of Borregaard, that he switched brand.
2 CONT
2 CONT Roald’s wife, Åse, was an only child. She lived in Soli in Tune and I remember we visited there when I was a child. Roald worked for Borregaard in Sarpsborg and drove a chemical truck back and forth between Sarpsborg and Sweden fo
2 CONC r a while.  I remember he used to buy cheap margarine and sugar in Sweden, the family would give him money to buy these fine but cheap items for them.
2 CONT
2 CONT Roald was also driving the internal mail car for Borregaard for a while I believe. Roald had his own business in Sannesund, it was a gas station with a kiosk and Roald would rust proof cars using the Tectyl chemicals.
2 CONT
2 CONT Roald and Åse had an apartment in Brevik by Sarpsborg and Åse kept it very clean and the furniture in the living room was covered by plastic for protection.
