1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.norwegianamerican.com/thea-foss/?fbclid=IwAR1n_ej7ZegEh3WgKXpsVJSLuVZson9XBZc11r4A-eqehjT38fY-lFRPz0Y
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth 1858 ref churchbook: https://media.digitalarkivet.no/view/359/33
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.foss.com/
2 CONT
2 CONT https://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thea_Foss
2 CONT
2 CONT https://forums.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSmcid=46847020&GRid=14662316&
2 CONT
2 CONT Thea Christiansen Foss (8 June 1858 – 7 June 1927) was the founder of Foss Maritime, the largest tugboat company in the western United States. She was the real-life person on which the fictional character "Tugboat Annie" (original
2 CONC ly portrayed on film in 1933 by Marie Dressler) was based.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thea Christiansen came to the United States from Eidsberg, Ostfold, Norway and married Norwegian immigrant Andrew Foss in Minneapolis, Minnesota in 1881. Thea Foss launched the future tugboat firm on the Tacoma waterfront in the s
2 CONC ummer of 1889. She started the Foss Launch Company, which eventually became the Seattle-based Foss Maritime Company.[1] Thea Foss had 9 children Mary, Katie, Issabell, lauren, Alexander, Tawann, Zach, Hanna, Chealsea. Thea Foss ha
2 CONC d 3 husbands 2 of them deserted her. Thea Foss died in Tacoma on the day before her 70th birthday.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT THEA’S BOATHOUSE
